IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-sched`

-- Tests for sgba-sched.l4 (First, Second and Third Schedules) and sgba-vintage.l4. Expected values are written from the text of the Schedules.

§ `Fixtures`

`apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` MEANS Apparatus WITH `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `capable of direct reception from a satellite` IS TRUE
`apparatus that can receive but not directly from a satellite` MEANS Apparatus WITH `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `capable of direct reception from a satellite` IS FALSE
`apparatus that cannot receive a broadcasting service` MEANS Apparatus WITH `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` IS FALSE, `capable of direct reception from a satellite` IS FALSE

§ `Vintage window of the Act: 25 September 2024 to 4 November 2026`

#ASSERT `the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` (Date 25 9 2024)
#ASSERT `the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` (Date 1 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` (Date 1 6 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` (Date 24 9 2024))
#ASSERT NOT (`the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` (Date 5 11 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` (Date 1 1 2011))

§ `First Schedule, item 1 and the interpretation paragraph`

#ASSERT `an apparatus is a television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system)` `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite`
#ASSERT NOT (`an apparatus is a television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system)` `apparatus that can receive but not directly from a satellite`)
#ASSERT NOT (`an apparatus is a television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system)` `apparatus that cannot receive a broadcasting service`)
-- dated: inside the window
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 1 6 2025) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 1 6 2025) `apparatus that can receive but not directly from a satellite` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- dated: the day before the window opens, the first day, the last day, the day after it closes
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 24 9 2024) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 25 9 2024) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 1 10 2026) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 5 11 2026) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING
-- before the deposited text: no past text was obtained, so the Schedule is not covered (including the dates around 1 January 2011)
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 31 12 2010) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 1 1 2011) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 2 1 2011) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 1 6 2015) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` (Date 1 6 2019) `apparatus that can receive directly from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Second Schedule, items 1 to 20 and the closing paragraph`

#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `free-to-air nationwide television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `free-to-air localised television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `free-to-air international television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `subscription nationwide television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `subscription localised television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `subscription international television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `special interest television services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `free-to-air nationwide radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `free-to-air localised radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `free-to-air international radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `subscription nationwide radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `subscription localised radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `subscription international radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `special interest radio services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `audiotext services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `videotext services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `teletext services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `video-on-demand services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `broadcast data services`)
#ASSERT `the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` (JUST `computer online services`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the delivery system is deemed a licensable broadcasting service by reason only of providing facilities or expertise for delivery` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the delivery system is deemed a licensable broadcasting service by reason only of providing facilities or expertise for delivery` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the service is specified in the Second Schedule on` (Date 1 6 2025) (JUST `audiotext services`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is specified in the Second Schedule on` (Date 1 6 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the service is specified in the Second Schedule on` (Date 24 9 2024) (JUST `audiotext services`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the service is specified in the Second Schedule on` (Date 5 11 2026) (JUST `audiotext services`) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Third Schedule`

#ASSERT `the person is named in the Third Schedule as a provider of a subscription nationwide television service` "StarHub Cable Vision Ltd."
#ASSERT `the person is named in the Third Schedule as a provider of a subscription nationwide television service` "SingNet Pte. Ltd."
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is named in the Third Schedule as a provider of a subscription nationwide television service` "Mediacorp Pte. Ltd.")
